  "description": "meme-id: black_lives_matter_meme; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts Black men in prison uniforms carrying large sacks, juxtaposed with the text 'black lives matter' and a sarcastic comment '>\"how\",\"why\"and \"to whom\" is unclear'. This visual and textual combination is a hate-based meme that uses the image of Black men in prison to imply that Black lives do not matter, or that the movement is hypocritical or irrelevant. It leverages a harmful stereotype associating Black people with criminality and incarceration, which is a form of racialized hate speech. The meme's intent is to delegitimize the Black Lives Matter movement by mocking its core message and implying that Black people are inherently criminal or undeserving of protection, thus falling under the category of hateful content targeting a specific racial group.",
